{"kind":"request","text":"CB-1: celld runs the `base` family.\n\nThe fact at main 4cef11d2. CF-1 makes `base` the default family of\n`dap install`. celld does not run it: `prepare-project.mjs` refuses a\n`base` plan (`docs/self-host-mac.md`, \"celld does not run `base`\").\nA celld room is `unpublished` or `repository-binding`, and it lacks\neach part of the list in that section: `leave` and the own-key\nrevoke, own agents, ordinary version 2 packages with publication\nprefixes, the final failed state of a claim, the fixed one-hour Git\nread token, and an archive. `bind-archive` refuses `no-repository`\nin those two families, which is the Directory 20 fault of ruling\n9658ed88.\n\nScene: an operator follows `docs/self-host-mac.md` on one Mac. The\nroom is of the `base` family, a member installs Counter in it, and\nthe owner binds an archive.\n\nBefore the code, send me one act:\n1. Each thing that stops celld from running `base` today, with the\n   file that holds it.\n2. What a `base` room needs from a host that celld lacks, and what\n   `--host none` means for publication prefixes and the archive.\n3. A proposal and its witness on the local celld Worker.\n\nWhen CB-1 lands, the list in `docs/self-host-mac.md` goes, and\n`prepare-project.mjs` plans `base` by default.\n\nOrder: after the cutover deployment and AE-1. NF-5 needs a local\n`base` room for the Counter witness of NF-7 (ruling bc826726). If\nthat witness cannot run without CB-1, say so in the NF-5 lane, and I\nmove CB-1 ahead.","body":{"conditions":"Planner accepts the pre-code act; prepare-project.mjs plans base by default; a local celld room of the base family installs Counter and binds an archive in a witness; docs/self-host-mac.md drops the list of missing parts; gate passes; checker reviews with the Security conclusion","target_head":"4cef11d2783efaa591fac197d9a2ba093004456e","target_ref":"refs/heads/main","target_repo":"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3","to":"feb90d36627c7f4466ef9473